Q3: producer/consumer using locks and condition variables

Build from lab2/ with the provided toolchain environment:
  mainframer.sh "make -C os && make -C apps/q3"

Run from lab2/ after building:
  make -C apps/q3 run PAIRS=3
Or run from lab2/bin/:
  dlxsim -x os.dlx.obj -a -u makeprocs.dlx.obj 3

The OS condition-variable implementation is in os/synch.c and
include/os/synch.h. Each condition stores its associated lock and a FIFO
queue of waiting processes. cond_wait enqueues the caller, releases the
associated lock, and sleeps atomically. cond_signal transfers the lock to
one waiter and then sleeps in the lock queue until it owns the lock again.
Both calls return SYNC_SUCCESS on success, as recommended by the handout.

The application uses one not_full condition for producers and one condition
for each possible next digit for consumers. A producer waits on not_full
while the circular buffer is full. A consumer waits on the condition for
its next digit while the buffer is empty or its expected digit is not at
the front. All conditions share the same buffer lock. The parent still uses
a semaphore only to wait for all children to finish, as required.

Q1, Q2, and Q3 produce executables with the same names in bin/. Clean and
rebuild the desired application when switching questions. The run target
only runs existing executables; it does not build them.

Before submission, clean every built application and the OS. For Q3:
  make -C apps/q3 clean
  make -C os clean
Preserve the supplied lib/share_memory.o.

References:
  ECE 695 Fall 2026 Laboratory #2 handout supplied by the user.
  Supplied OS lock/semaphore code, apps/example, and Q1 in this workspace.
  Implementation assistance: OpenAI Codex in this workspace.
No external web sources were used.

Validation:
Built the OS and Q3 in a temporary /tmp copy. Runs with 1, 3, and 4 pairs
used default simulator memory; 8 pairs used -m 0x1000000. Checked each
process's 0123456789 sequence, FIFO removals, buffer capacity, message
counts, and graceful termination. Inputs 0, 16, abc, and -1 were rejected.
Q1 and Q2 also passed three-pair regression runs with the modified OS.
Generated test artifacts remain outside the source tree.
